# s72_security_part2.oot — (Part 2 of s72_security.oot)
# Continuation of `openOODA/audit/s72_security.oot`.

## Attack results (product host)
Verdict key:

- **BLOCK** = emit-c **and** check `ERR\tsecret` + rc≠0
- **ALLOW** = both rc=0, no `ERR\tsecret` (correct for pass / FP cases)
- **FN** = allowed when unquoted SECRET reached `sys_exec` argv
- **FP** = refused when secret spelling was only in a string
- **HIDE** = quote/escape skip consumed a following unquoted SECRET

Host: `OODAC=/home/jeryd/Projects/openOODA/ooda/oodac/oodac`
Probes: `/tmp/s72_sec_1RZEDK/z*.oo` (ephemeral).
Harness: `ooda/scripts/s72_sys_exec_last_arg_smoke.oo` **exit 0**.

### Z1 — SECRET last argv fail-closed
| # | Shape | emit-c | check | emit-llvm | Verdict |
|---|-------|--------|-------|-----------|---------|
| 1 | `sys_exec(sys, "sh", "-c", tok)` last IDENT | rc=1 SECRET tok | rc=1 SECRET tok | rc=1 SECRET tok | **BLOCK** |
| 2 | `sys_exec(sys, "echo", tok)` last = a2 | rc=1 SECRET tok | rc=1 SECRET tok | rc=1 SECRET tok | **BLOCK** |
| 3 | `sys_exec(sys, tok)` last = a1 | rc=1 SECRET tok | rc=1 SECRET tok | rc=1 SECRET tok | **BLOCK** |
| 4 | `sys_exec(sys, "sh", "-c", tok, "true")` mid argv | rc=1 SECRET tok | rc=1 SECRET tok | rc=1 SECRET tok | **BLOCK** (scan/check; not last-span) |
| 5 | `let x = tok; sys_exec(..., x)` alias last | rc=1 SECRET x | rc=1 SECRET x | rc=1 SECRET x | **BLOCK** |
| 6 | `sys_exec(..., "echo " + tok)` concat last | rc=1 SECRET tok | rc=1 SECRET tok | rc=1 SECRET tok | **BLOCK** (scan; last not cap-ident) |
| 7 | `sys_exec(..., wrap(tok))` nested | rc=1 SECRET tok | rc=1 SECRET tok | rc=1 SECRET tok | **BLOCK** (scan) |
| 8 | `sys_exec(p, "sh", "-c", tok)` `&ProcessCap` | rc=1 SECRET tok | rc=1 SECRET tok | rc=1 SECRET tok | **BLOCK** |
| F | `fixtures/secret_sys_exec_fail` | rc=1 SECRET token | rc=1 SECRET token | rc=1 SECRET token | **BLOCK** |
| F | `fixtures/secret_sys_exec_argv_fail` | rc=1 SECRET token | rc=1 SECRET token | rc=1 SECRET token | **BLOCK** |
| C | `fixtures/secret_sys_exec_pass` public last | rc=0 | rc=0 | rc=0 | **ALLOW** |
| C | `fixtures/secret_sys_exec_argv_pass` | rc=0 | rc=0 | rc=0 | **ALLOW** |

**FN count on assigned last-IDENT argv: 0.**

Why last-arg exists: a1/a2 are only the first two C args after the cap.
`sys_exec(sys, "sh", "-c", tok)` lowers to
`sys, oo_str_lit("sh"), oo_str_lit("-c"), tok` — tok is **a3**.
Last-arg + full-args scan are the emit rails for that slot. Check/LLVM
use token `c_secret_scan_call(..., want=1, eq_only=false)` (any argi≥1).

### Z2 — quote-split cannot hide unquoted SECRET
Product join is `", "` between lowered args. Last-arg and the 7.1 walker
share the same `in_str` + `\\` skip + paren `depth` rules. Live shapes
go through `sys_exec` so **both** last-arg and scan see the text.

| # | Source shape (after SECRET tag) | emit-c | check | llvm | HIDE? |
|---|----------------------------------|--------|-------|------|-------|
| Q0 | last `"echo hello, tok, SECRET"` (no IDENT) | ALLOW | ALLOW | ALLOW | n/a (**no FP**) |
| Q1 | `"echo,foo"` then last `tok` | BLOCK | BLOCK | BLOCK | **no** |
| Q2 | `"a,b" + "c,d"` then last `tok` | BLOCK | BLOCK | BLOCK | **no** |
| Q3 | `"foo\\"` then last `tok` | BLOCK | BLOCK | BLOCK | **no** |
| Q4 | `"foo\"bar"` then last `tok` | BLOCK | BLOCK | BLOCK | **no** |
| Q5 | `"\\"` then last `tok` | BLOCK | BLOCK | BLOCK | **no** |
| Q6 | `"/* tok */"` then last `tok` | BLOCK | BLOCK | BLOCK | **no** |
| Q7 | `"//"` then last `tok` | BLOCK | BLOCK | BLOCK | **no** |
| Q8 | `"foo\\\"x"` then last `tok` | BLOCK | BLOCK | BLOCK | **no** |
| Q9 | `"\""` then last `tok` | BLOCK | BLOCK | BLOCK | **no** |
| Q10 | `sys_exec(sys, "tok")` string-only last | ALLOW | ALLOW | ALLOW | n/a (**no FP**) |

Python replica of the last-arg walker on product-shaped C text
(`sys, oo_str_lit("echo,foo"), tok` and every Q3–Q9 escape) always
returns `tok` as the last span (cap-ident). Quoted last with interior
commas returns the whole `oo_str_lit("…")` (not a cap-ident) → last-arg
rail skips; scan stays `in_str` → no FP.

Why hide is hard on product emit: `c_escape_str_text` always emits
well-formed C (`\\`, `\"`, `\\n`, `\\t`, 2-char controls). Even
backslash run before `"` closes the string; odd run (`\"`) is content.
Following `", tok` is outside the string. Nested `f(a, b)` commas sit
at `depth>0` and do not move `last_start`.

**HIDE count: 0** on live well-formed emit text.

### Z3 — no fail-open if last-arg helper returns empty
Caller skip (the hole if live):

```
let last = c_sys_exec_last_arg(args);
if last != "" && c_arg_is_cap_ident(last) { refuse(last); }
```

Helper returns (source + replica):

| Input | Return | Empty? |
|-------|--------|--------|
| `n == 0` | `"oo_str_lit(\"\")"` placeholder | **no** |
| `last_start >= n` | `args` (full) | only if `args == ""` (already handled) |
| `str_slice` empty | `args` | same |
| otherwise | `str_slice(args, last_start, n)` | **no** for `last_start < n` |

`last_start` starts at 0 and is assigned only to a `j < n` (first
non-space after a top-level comma). So `last_start >= n` and
`out == ""` are **dead** for `n > 0`. Replica over empty / trailing
comma / all-spaces / `,,,` / quoted commas: **0 empty returns**.

If the helper **did** return `""` with `args != ""`:

- last-arg rail would skip (`if last != ""`)
- `c_guard_scan_idents` still walks full `args` (7.1 backup; not reopened)
- check/LLVM token walk still refuses last IDENT (argi≥1)

Live proof that skip of the last-arg rail is not a FN: concat / wrap
last spans are **not** cap-idents (`c_arg_is_cap_ident` false) — same
skip as empty — and still **BLOCK** on emit-c + check + llvm.

`sys_exec(sys)` (no argv): helper returns `sys` (single span, not empty).
No SECRET in args → ALLOW. (Arity residual: `c_args_drop_first` with no
comma returns the cap as argv — **not** a secret FN.)

**Empty-helper fail-open count: 0.**

